cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use anySeg in research or software, please cite it."
title: "anySeg, fast segmentation of text into tokens and sentences"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shkarin
    given-names: Sergey
    email: kouki.sergey@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/SergeyShk/anySeg"
url: "https://sergeyshk.github.io/anySeg/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - nlp
  - tokenization
  - sentence segmentation
  - universal dependencies
  - russian
  - rust
abstract: "anySeg segments text into tokens and sentences with their positions in the source text. The core is written in Rust, the package has a Python API and no dependencies. The text is never changed: every token and sentence is a span of the original string, and tokens follow the conventions of Universal Dependencies."
